# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev (Vite auto-loads it; the template's
# own .gitignore already excludes `.env.local` — never commit real values).
# In CI, these are injected as build-time values by
# .github/workflows/frontend-deploy.yml, read from GitHub Environment
# variables, not from a committed file.
#
# Any variable exposed to browser code MUST be prefixed VITE_ — this is a
# real security boundary, not a style convention: Vite only inlines
# VITE_-prefixed vars into the shipped bundle, so anything without the
# prefix never reaches client JS, while anything WITH it should be treated
# as fully public (visible via devtools) the moment it's used.
#
# ── Why five separate base URLs instead of one ──────────────────────────
# Locally, each service is its own Spring Boot process on its own port
# with no path prefix (see order-saga-orchestrator/src/main/resources/
# application.yml's own port map comment: order-service=8080,
# fraud-detection=8082, analytics=8084, order-saga-orchestrator=8089,
# search-indexer=8090). In AWS, all five sit behind ONE Application Load
# Balancer on ONE hostname, split by PATH prefix instead of port —
# cloud/cdk/lib/app-services-stack.ts's `SERVICE_SPECS` array is the
# source of truth (`/orders/*`, `/fraud/*`, `/analytics/*`, `/saga/*`,
# `/search/*`), and each container's SERVER_SERVLET_CONTEXT_PATH is set
# to match, so the app-internal route (e.g. `/api/orders`) ends up
# reachable at `<alb-dns>/orders/api/orders` externally. Baking the
# *entire* origin+prefix into each env var (rather than hardcoding `/api/
# orders` and switching on `import.meta.env.PROD` in code) means the
# `api/*.ts` client files never need an if/else for environment — they
# always just append `/api/orders` etc. to whatever base this file gives
# them, and only the .env VALUES differ between local and prod.
VITE_ORDERS_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
VITE_SAGA_API_URL=http://localhost:8089
VITE_ANALYTICS_API_URL=http://localhost:8084
VITE_FRAUD_API_URL=http://localhost:8082
VITE_SEARCH_API_URL=http://localhost:8090

# Production values (set as GitHub Environment variables, not here) look
# like: VITE_ORDERS_API_URL=https://<alb-dns-from-cdk-output>/orders
